---
name: dev-sanity-task
version: 2.2.0
description: lead sanity check assignment for the member that fills the dev-sanity role (resolve-role dev-sanity). task_id is the sanity check bead. The member splits the checked bead per numbered deliverable (sanity-split), runs LLM and JEV checkers per deliverable and a selected merge with lint alongside, then reports PASS or FAIL. Not QA.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - sprint
  - worktree_path
  - branch
  - commit
  - base
  - pr_number
  - pr_url
  - primary_checkout
  - lead
  - cc
  - lint_command
metadata:
  type: dev-sanity-task
  tags:
    - stage:dev-sanity
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: dev-sanity-start
    stage: dev-sanity
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="dev-sanity">
  <description><![CDATA[Sanity check `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`: nothing skipped, no obvious errors, lint passes. This is not QA.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <pr number="{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr>
  <lint-command><![CDATA[{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}]]></lint-command>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Run `test -n "{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}" && test -n "{{ pr_url | string | cdata_escape }}"` or refuse `SANITY.PR_REQUIRED`. Then run `gh pr view {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} --json baseRefName,headRefOid --jq '.baseRefName + " " + .headRefOid'`; require base `{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}` equal to `bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.pr_target'` (else `SANITY.PR_TARGET_MISMATCH`) and head `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`. Run `git fetch origin && git log --format=%H origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}..{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }} | grep -q .` or refuse `SANITY.ZERO_DELTA`; run `test -z "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=no | grep -v -e '^?? \.beads\.gate\.lock$' -e ' \.sc-compose/')"` or refuse `SANITY.DIRTY_TREE` (the ignored paths are `IGNORED_STATUS_PATHS` in `scripts/assignment-gates.py`); run `bd history {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` and refuse `SANITY_FROZEN` when it records a prior PASS. Reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Otherwise claim and start the check.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[When it prints `false` the bead is not ready: do not claim it and do not start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (normally `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` still open), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Report it with `atm send {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`: the bead, why it is not ready, and which bead or agent has to move. Then wait.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Follow `.claude/agents/dev-sanity.md`, the canonical coordinator. Run sanity-split once and send identical assignments to both reviewers concurrently. Preserve both raw result arrays. Record each reviewer's completion epoch when its last reply or timeout envelope arrives, before merging or waiting for shared lint; merge it as soon as it finishes with `--started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch>`. Do not append history until selected merge determines the final verdict. Build one strict selection array with one entry per deliverable, recording the selected start epoch when selection begins and completion epoch when `selection.json` is written. Invoke selected merge only as `sanity-merge ... --reviewer sanity-selected --started-at <its-start-epoch> --completed-at <its-completion-epoch> --llm-vars <sanity-llm-vars.json> --jev-vars <sanity-jev-vars.json> --selection <selection.json>`; stdin is ignored. Append history in exact order LLM, JEV, SEL, passing every row the selected verdict as `--final-verdict`; if selection or selected merge cannot run use `CANNOT_RUN` and still append LLM/JEV. Copy only SEL vars to `<scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json` for steps e/e1. Exit 4 waits for shared lint and retries reuse supplied epochs; selected cannot-run routes to e2.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[PASS: For each `checker_defect`, append the selection entry to the matching workflow class bead (or report it to the lead) and cite it in notes. Then close the bead and the task together: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "PASS at <sha>"` and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/dev-sanity-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json` with `verdict` PASS. Closing the bead releases every dev bead that required `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`.]]></step>
    <step id="e1"><![CDATA[Selected FAIL only: the sanity bead must stay **open**, because closing it would release dependent dev beads. Preserve every finding unchanged. For each `checker_defect`, append the selection entry to the matching workflow class bead (or report it to the lead) and cite it in notes. Before closing this task, run this exact command against the merge-created vars file; it creates one open `bug` child per finding under `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`, copies the report fields verbatim to child metadata and description, and adds each declared inter-finding blocking edge. Use `--reviewer sc-sanity-selected`; each child records the selected LLM/JEV source. Checker defects create no child; the selection record and workflow-issue class bead carry their evidence. Do not reopen or otherwise edit the checked parent:

```bash
{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/sanity-create-findings \
  --task {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --bead {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} \
  --vars <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json \
  --reviewer sc-sanity-selected \
  --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY" > <scratch>/sanity-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-finding-children.json
```

`sanity-create-findings` creates finding children and only their declared inter-finding prerequisite edges. It never creates a finding-sanity gate or adds an edge to another planned sprint: `sprints.jsonl` is the sole authority for sprint-to-sprint dependencies.

The script gives each child the severity priority from `plan_contract` (blocking P1, important P2, minor P4) and copies the parent's required difficulty. The parent/child hierarchy itself is the parent closure gate; `bd` rejects a parent-to-child `blocks` edge because that would deadlock the child. For each report `depends_on` selector, the script creates `<dependent-finding-child> --blocks--> <prerequisite-finding-child>`, preventing the dependent fix from closing first. It adds the ordered `finding_bead_ids` array to the same vars file used by `atm task close`, so the final report links directly to every child; do not write those ids to parent notes because the graph is authoritative. Return the sanity bead to the queue with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "FAIL at <sha>: <n> findings"`, then close the task with the same `atm task close … completed` command and `verdict` FAIL. A failure to create or wire every child is cannot-run, not a completed FAIL. {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} reviews the created child beads, then follows the existing process to reopen the parent and assign the dev fix; the lead may overrule, amend, split, or reassign children. The parent cannot close until all children close; only then may final parent closure occur, after which the next sanity run is ready.{% if cc and cc != lead %} Copy the verdict line to `{{ cc | string | cdata_escape }}` with a plain `atm send {{ cc | string | cdata_escape }} --stdin`.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="e2"><![CDATA[If the selected check cannot run (plan not splittable, worktree missing, commit not pushed, a check timed out or was rejected twice), reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If no class matches, report the signature to {{ lead | string | cdata_escape }} for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "<code>; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`.]]></step>
    <step id="e3"><![CDATA[After the selected task close, render the last sanity-run-history output with `templates/sanity-run-table.md.j2`, as the canonical coordinator specifies. History is appended in exact reviewer order LLM, JEV, SEL (including CANNOT_RUN), with shared run_id, explicit reviewer/commit, each reviewer's own UTC timing, and the same selected `--final-verdict` on every row. `--limit 10` means newest ten runs, with all three rows kept together. `Pick` appears only for SEL as `=<agree> L<llm> J<jev> R<rerun>` (zero L/J/R omitted) and `D<n>` for checker defects. `Match` is ✓/✗ for LLM/JEV agreement with the final verdict and — for SEL or historical rows. Include the complete compact `S | PR | R | Pick | Find | Result | Match | Done | Iter` table as Markdown directly in the user-visible completion reply before reading ATM again. No full task IDs. Local time is display-only, derived from UTC. Report `SANITY.STATUS_TABLE_UNAVAILABLE` and the error if append/render fails, without changing any verdict. Pre-dispatch refusals have no reviewer row.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[After the close and the required user-visible completion reply in step e3 (whenever reviewer results exist), read ATM again.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
